-- =====================================================================================================================
-- AptRun: AWS DATABASE UPDATE  (everything after aws-db-update-2026-11-06.sql: C# & .NET and ASP.NET Core interview questions)
--
-- Brings an EXISTING AptRun database up to date WITHOUT replacing it. It is the SQL equivalent of
--       php artisan migrate --force
--   (2026_11_19_100000 add_dotnet_interview_questions)
-- and it records that migration in the `migrations` table, so a later `php artisan migrate` will not run it again.
--
-- WHAT IT DOES   (data only: no schema change, no new table)
--   Two new Backend stacks exist in the Vault AI Interview AND the Mock AI Interview: "C# & .NET" (csharp_dotnet) and "ASP.NET Core"
--   (aspnet_core). The stacks are catalogue config (config/curated_interview_domains.php, deployed with the code); this file adds their QUESTIONS:
--     curated_set_questions    90 rows  (2 stacks x 3 series x 3 sets x 5)  -> each stack opens to students by itself
--     mock_interview_questions 30 rows  (2 stacks x 3 rounds x 5)
--
-- SAFE TO RUN TWICE: every row is inserted only if no row exists yet for the same (set, position) / (stack, round, position), so a
-- question a superadmin has edited since is never overwritten and a second run adds nothing. (php artisan migrate would restore the
-- shipped wording of an untouched position; this file deliberately leaves existing rows alone.)
--
-- BEFORE YOU RUN IT: take a backup, and deploy the code first (the stacks must exist in config for the questions to show).
-- Generated from database/seeders/data/{vault,mock}_questions/dotnet_*.php by the same data the migration reads.
-- =====================================================================================================================

SET NAMES utf8mb4;
START TRANSACTION;

