SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 1, 1, 'Explain value types versus reference types in C#. Where do they live in memory, how does assignment behave for each, and when would you choose a struct over a class?', 'technical', 180, 'Value types (struct, enum, primitives) copy their data on assignment and are usually stored inline (stack or inside the containing object); reference types hold a reference to a heap object, so assignment copies the reference. Structs suit small, immutable, short-lived data (under about 16 bytes); large or mutable structs cause copying costs and surprising bugs. Mention boxing when a value type is treated as object.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
