SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 1, 2, 'Strings in C# are immutable. What does that mean in practice, why is repeated concatenation in a loop a problem, and when do you reach for StringBuilder?', 'technical', 180, 'Every concatenation creates a new string object, so a loop of N appends is O(N squared) in copying and allocates garbage. StringBuilder keeps a mutable buffer and is the right tool for many appends; a handful of concatenations or string interpolation is fine. Mention string interning and that immutability makes strings safe to share across threads.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
