SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 1, 3, 'Compare an abstract class with an interface. Since C# 8 interfaces can have default implementations, so when do you still prefer an abstract class?', 'technical', 180, 'An abstract class can hold state (fields), constructors and protected members and gives a shared base with partial implementation, but a class has only one base. Interfaces define a contract that many unrelated types implement; default interface methods help evolve an interface without breaking implementers but cannot hold instance state. Prefer abstract classes for a real is-a hierarchy with shared state, interfaces for capabilities and for testability.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
