SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 1, 5, 'What are nullable reference types in C# 8 and later? How do the ? and ! operators, ?. and ?? help, and why do they not remove NullReferenceException completely?', 'technical', 180, 'Nullable reference types add compile-time flow analysis: string is non-nullable by intent, string? may be null, and the compiler warns on possible null dereference. ?. short-circuits on null, ?? supplies a default, ! suppresses a warning (a promise by the developer). It is only static analysis with warnings, so legacy code, reflection, deserialisation or a misused ! can still throw at runtime.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
