SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 2, 3, 'What is the difference between IEnumerable<T> and IQueryable<T>, and why does it matter when you query a database with Entity Framework?', 'technical', 180, 'IEnumerable runs LINQ in memory using delegates; IQueryable builds an expression tree that the provider (EF Core) translates to SQL so filtering happens in the database. Calling AsEnumerable or ToList too early pulls the whole table and filters in memory. Keep the query as IQueryable until the filters, ordering and paging are applied.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
