SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 2, 4, 'Explain what async and await actually do. Does await create a new thread? How does Task differ from Thread?', 'technical', 180, 'async methods are compiled into a state machine; await yields control to the caller while the awaited operation (usually I/O) is pending and resumes the method afterwards, without blocking a thread. It does not create a thread by itself. A Task represents a unit of asynchronous work or a future result, scheduled on the thread pool or completed by I/O callbacks, while Thread is an OS-level thread that is expensive to create.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
