SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 2, 5, 'What are delegates, events, Func<> and Action<>? How do lambda expressions capture variables, and what is a closure?', 'technical', 180, 'A delegate is a type-safe function pointer; Func<> returns a value and Action<> returns void. An event is a delegate with restricted access (only the owner can raise it, others can only subscribe or unsubscribe). Lambdas capture variables, not values, so a captured loop variable or a long-lived subscription can keep objects alive or behave unexpectedly; the closure is the compiler-generated class holding captured variables.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
