SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 3, 1, 'Explain the CLR, IL and the JIT compiler. How do .NET Framework, .NET Core, .NET Standard and modern .NET (5 and later) relate to each other?', 'technical', 180, 'C# compiles to Intermediate Language plus metadata in an assembly; the CLR loads it and the JIT compiles IL to machine code at run time. .NET Framework is the Windows-only original; .NET Core is the cross-platform rewrite, unified as .NET 5 and later; .NET Standard was an API contract for sharing libraries across them and is largely replaced by targeting modern .NET. New work should target a supported LTS version.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
