SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 3, 2, 'How does the .NET garbage collector work? Explain generations, the Large Object Heap and the role of IDisposable and finalizers.', 'technical', 180, 'The GC is generational (gen 0, 1, 2): most objects die young, so gen 0 is collected often and cheaply; objects of about 85,000 bytes or more go to the LOH, collected with gen 2. The GC frees managed memory only; unmanaged resources (files, sockets, handles) need IDisposable with using or Dispose, with a finalizer only as a safety net because finalizable objects survive extra collections.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
