SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 3, 3, 'What is the difference between throw; and throw ex; in a catch block? How should exceptions be designed and handled in a .NET application?', 'technical', 180, 'throw; rethrows and preserves the original stack trace; throw ex; resets it, hiding where the error began. Catch only what you can handle, use specific exception types, use finally or using for cleanup, do not use exceptions for normal control flow (they are slow), and log with the full exception. Exception filters (when) allow conditional catching without unwinding.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
