SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s1-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 3, 5, 'How do you make shared state thread-safe in C#? Compare lock, Interlocked, ConcurrentDictionary and immutable data, and explain how a deadlock happens.', 'technical', 180, 'lock gives mutual exclusion for a critical section; Interlocked offers atomic operations on single variables; concurrent collections handle concurrent access internally; immutable data avoids sharing mutable state at all. A deadlock occurs when threads hold locks and wait for each other in a cycle; prevent it with a consistent lock ordering, short critical sections, no awaits or callbacks inside locks, and timeouts.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
