SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 1, 1, 'Explain generic constraints (where T : class, struct, new(), an interface) and covariance and contravariance. Why is IEnumerable<out T> covariant but List<T> not?', 'technical', 180, 'Constraints let generic code call members or create instances of T safely. Covariance (out) lets IEnumerable<Dog> be used as IEnumerable<Animal> because it only produces T; contravariance (in) lets Action<Animal> be used as Action<Dog> because it only consumes T. List<T> both reads and writes T, so allowing covariance would let you add a Cat to a list of Dogs and break type safety.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
