SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 1, 3, 'A class implements two interfaces that declare the same method name. How do explicit interface implementations solve this, and what is the downside of default interface methods and multiple inheritance of behaviour?', 'technical', 180, 'Explicit implementation (void IA.Do()) provides a separate body per interface and is reachable only through that interface type, resolving the ambiguity. Default interface methods can create diamond-like conflicts that the compiler forces you to resolve explicitly, and they hide logic in interfaces; keep them for backward-compatible interface evolution, not as a substitute for composition.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
