SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 1, 4, 'How do extension methods work and how does the compiler resolve them? What are their limitations and risks in a shared codebase?', 'technical', 180, 'An extension method is a static method in a static class whose first parameter uses this; calls compile to a normal static call, so they cannot access private members or be overridden, and an instance method with the same signature always wins. Risks: name collisions across namespaces, discoverability through using directives, extending types you do not own in surprising ways, and null receivers because the call works on null.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
