SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 1, 5, 'When is a struct a good design? Discuss readonly struct, the in modifier, defensive copies and why large mutable structs are dangerous.', 'technical', 180, 'Small immutable structs avoid heap allocations and improve locality. A mutable struct stored in a readonly field or returned from a property gets copied, so mutations are silently lost; large structs are expensive to copy on every call. readonly struct lets the compiler skip defensive copies, and in passes by reference without allowing modification, useful for hot paths.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
