SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 2, 3, 'What are IAsyncEnumerable<T> and await foreach, and when do they beat returning a List<T>? How does yield return work behind the scenes?', 'technical', 180, 'IAsyncEnumerable streams results asynchronously one item at a time, so large result sets or slow producers do not need to be buffered fully in memory, and the consumer can start early. yield return makes the compiler generate a state machine that resumes after each item. Remember to support cancellation with [EnumeratorCancellation] and to dispose of the underlying resources.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
