SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 2, 4, 'Explain the difference between CPU-bound and I/O-bound work. When is Task.Run appropriate, and why is wrapping I/O in Task.Run inside an ASP.NET Core request a mistake?', 'technical', 180, 'I/O-bound work should use true async APIs, freeing the thread while waiting. CPU-bound work occupies a thread, so in a desktop app Task.Run offloads it from the UI thread. In ASP.NET Core a request already runs on a thread-pool thread, so Task.Run only adds a hop and pool pressure without benefit; use async I/O and, for heavy CPU work, a background queue or separate worker.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
