SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 2, 5, 'A LINQ query over an in-memory list of 100,000 items is slow. Which patterns cause poor performance (multiple enumeration, Count() > 0, nested loops via Where inside Select) and how would you fix them?', 'technical', 180, 'Common problems: enumerating the same deferred query repeatedly, using Count() > 0 instead of Any(), nested Where lookups that are O(n squared) instead of building a Dictionary or ToLookup first, sorting repeatedly, and allocating many intermediate objects. Fix by materialising once, using hash-based lookups, choosing GroupBy or Join appropriately and measuring with BenchmarkDotNet before optimising.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
