SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 3, 1, 'Compare workstation and server garbage collection, concurrent GC and why calling GC.Collect() is usually wrong. Which tools show GC behaviour in a running app?', 'technical', 180, 'Workstation GC favours responsiveness on a single heap; server GC uses a heap and thread per core for throughput, with higher memory use. Background (concurrent) GC reduces gen 2 pauses. Forcing collections disrupts the generational tuning and usually hurts performance. Use dotnet-counters, dotnet-trace, PerfView and runtime metrics (gen 0/1/2 counts, pause time, allocation rate) to observe.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
