SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 3, 3, 'How do Span<T>, Memory<T> and ArrayPool<T> reduce allocations? Give an example where you would use them and a limitation of Span<T>.', 'technical', 180, 'Span<T> is a stack-only view over contiguous memory (arrays, stackalloc, strings) allowing slicing without copying, ideal for parsing; Memory<T> is the heap-storable counterpart for async code; ArrayPool rents and returns buffers to avoid repeated large allocations. Span is a ref struct, so it cannot be a field of a class, be captured in lambdas or live across await.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
