SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s2-set3', 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 3, 5, 'How do NuGet package versioning, transitive dependencies and assembly binding cause problems such as version conflicts in a large solution, and how do you manage them?', 'technical', 180, 'Different projects may pull different versions of the same package transitively, and the highest version generally wins, which can break a library built against an older API. Manage it with central package management (Directory.Packages.props), lock files, consistent target frameworks, semantic versioning discipline and CI checks for vulnerabilities and conflicts. Older .NET Framework projects used binding redirects for the same problem.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
