SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s3-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 3, 1, 1, 'Design a Money value object in C# for a payments system. What should it contain, how do you handle equality, rounding and currency mismatches, and why decimal rather than double?', 'architecture', 180, 'An immutable record struct or class holding Amount (decimal) and Currency, with value equality, validation in the constructor and operations (Add, Subtract) that reject mismatched currencies. decimal is base-10 with exact representation of money values while double has binary rounding errors. Define a rounding policy (banker rounding versus away-from-zero) and keep minor units explicit when storing or serialising.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
