SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s3-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 3, 1, 2, 'How would you implement a thread-safe lazy singleton in C#? Compare Lazy<T>, static initialisation and double-checked locking, and say when a singleton is a bad idea.', 'technical', 180, 'Static readonly initialisation or Lazy<T> (thread-safe by default with LazyThreadSafetyMode.ExecutionAndPublication) are the simple correct options; hand-written double-checked locking needs volatile and is easy to get wrong. Singletons hide dependencies and make testing hard; prefer dependency injection with a singleton lifetime and keep the type stateless or thread-safe.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
