SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s3-set1', 'csharp_dotnet', 3, 1, 5, 'Review this code: foreach (var order in orders) { Task.Run(() => Process(order)); } return Ok(); What problems do you see?', 'scenario', 180, 'It is fire-and-forget: exceptions are unobserved and lost, the response returns before work finishes, there is no cancellation or throttling, and starting one task per order can flood the thread pool. Process may also capture loop state incorrectly in older C# versions. Use a background queue (Channel or hosted service) with limited concurrency, or await Task.WhenAll with a bounded degree of parallelism and proper error handling.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
