SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s3-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 3, 2, 1, 'Design a producer-consumer pipeline in .NET with System.Threading.Channels. How do bounded channels give backpressure, and how would you shut it down gracefully?', 'architecture', 180, 'Producers write to a Channel<T>; consumers read with ReadAllAsync. A bounded channel with a capacity makes WriteAsync wait (or drop, depending on BoundedChannelFullMode) when consumers are slower, preventing unbounded memory growth. For shutdown, call Writer.Complete() so consumers drain and finish, and use a CancellationToken for forced stop, awaiting all consumer tasks.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
