SELECT 'backend-csharp_dotnet-s3-set2', 'csharp_dotnet', 3, 2, 4, 'A Dictionary shared by several threads occasionally throws or loops forever. Explain why, and what ConcurrentDictionary guarantees and does not guarantee (for example about GetOrAdd).', 'technical', 180, 'Dictionary is not thread-safe; concurrent writes can corrupt its internal buckets, causing exceptions or infinite loops. ConcurrentDictionary makes individual operations atomic, but the value factory in GetOrAdd or AddOrUpdate may run more than once and its result is discarded when another thread wins, so factories must be side-effect free or wrapped in Lazy<T>.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
