SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s1-set1', 'aspnet_core', 1, 1, 2, 'Explain the three service lifetimes in ASP.NET Core dependency injection: Transient, Scoped and Singleton. What is a captive dependency and why is it a bug?', 'technical', 180, 'Transient creates a new instance each time, Scoped one per request scope, Singleton one for the application. A captive dependency is a longer-lived service holding a shorter-lived one (for example a singleton injecting a scoped DbContext), keeping it alive across requests and causing stale data, concurrency bugs and memory leaks. Scope validation in development detects it.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
