SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s1-set1', 'aspnet_core', 1, 1, 4, 'How does routing work in ASP.NET Core? Explain endpoint routing, attribute routes, route constraints and the main model binding sources such as FromBody, FromQuery and FromRoute.', 'technical', 180, 'Endpoint routing matches the request to an endpoint early (UseRouting) and executes it later (UseEndpoints or MapControllers). Attribute routes such as [HttpGet("orders/{id:int}")] define templates with constraints. Model binding fills parameters from route values, query string, headers, form or body; [ApiController] infers sources (complex types from body, simple from route or query).', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
