SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s1-set2', 'aspnet_core', 1, 2, 5, 'Why should controller actions be async? Explain how Kestrel and the thread pool serve requests and what happens when you block threads with synchronous calls.', 'technical', 180, 'Async I/O frees the thread while waiting for the database or HTTP calls, letting the same threads serve many more requests. Kestrel uses the thread pool; blocking calls (.Result, Thread.Sleep, synchronous I/O) hold threads, and under load the pool starves, latency grows and requests time out. Use async APIs through the whole call chain.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
