SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s2-set2', 'aspnet_core', 2, 2, 2, 'How do transactions work in EF Core? Explain SaveChanges atomicity, explicit transactions, execution strategies with retries and DbContext pooling.', 'technical', 180, 'SaveChanges wraps all pending changes in one transaction. Use BeginTransaction for several SaveChanges or mixed commands. With a retrying execution strategy (transient failure resilience for cloud SQL), wrap the whole unit of work in strategy.ExecuteAsync so it can be retried safely. DbContext pooling reuses context instances to cut allocation cost, so no per-request state must be stored in the context.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
