SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s2-set3', 'aspnet_core', 2, 3, 1, 'Explain JWT validation in depth: signature, issuer, audience, lifetime and clock skew. How do refresh tokens, key rotation and token revocation work, and how do OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect fit in?', 'technical', 180, 'The API validates signature with the issuer keys (JWKS), plus issuer, audience, expiry and not-before with a small clock skew. Short-lived access tokens are paired with refresh tokens stored securely and rotated; key rotation uses multiple valid keys during transition; revocation needs a deny list or short lifetimes because JWTs are self-contained. OAuth 2.0 delegates access, OpenID Connect adds identity; use an identity provider rather than building your own.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
