SELECT 'backend-aspnet_core-s3-set2', 'aspnet_core', 3, 2, 2, 'Two users edit the same record at the same time. How do optimistic concurrency and concurrency tokens in EF Core detect the conflict, and how should the API and UI resolve it?', 'scenario', 180, 'A RowVersion or concurrency token column is included in the UPDATE condition; if another user changed the row, zero rows are affected and EF throws DbUpdateConcurrencyException. The API returns 409 or 412, the client can reload the latest values and show a merge or overwrite choice. Use pessimistic locks only when conflicts are frequent and costly.', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
