SELECT 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 1, 'What is the difference between a class and a struct in C#? Give an example of when you would use each.', 'technical', 180, 'Classes are reference types allocated on the heap and copied by reference; structs are value types copied by value, best for small immutable data such as a point or a money amount. Structs cannot inherit from another class, and large or mutable structs hurt performance and cause confusing copies.', 'document', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
