SELECT 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 2, 'Explain the difference between an abstract class and an interface in C#. When do you use which?', 'technical', 180, 'An abstract class can contain fields, constructors and implemented methods and is used for a shared base in an is-a hierarchy; an interface declares a contract that unrelated classes can implement, and a class can implement many interfaces. Prefer interfaces for loose coupling and testing, abstract classes when sharing state and behaviour.', 'document', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
