SELECT 'csharp_dotnet', 1, 5, 'Explain virtual, override and new (method hiding) in C#. What is polymorphism and how does it relate to them?', 'technical', 180, 'A virtual method can be overridden in a derived class and the runtime picks the implementation by the actual object type, which is polymorphism. new hides a base method instead, so the called method depends on the compile-time variable type, which often causes bugs. Use override for polymorphic behaviour.', 'document', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
