SELECT 'csharp_dotnet', 2, 5, 'What are delegates and events in C#? Give an example of using Action, Func and an event handler.', 'technical', 180, 'A delegate is a type-safe reference to a method. Action represents a method returning void and Func a method returning a value. An event is built on a delegate and lets a publisher notify subscribers (button clicked, order placed) while preventing outsiders from invoking it; subscribers should unsubscribe to avoid leaks.', 'document', NULL, NOW(), NOW() FROM DUAL
